\viewkind4\uc1 \f1\fs20\b WORKSHEET\b0\par
\f1\fs32\b The Firstfruit and the Honest Weight\b0\fs24\par
\f1\fs20 Torah: Deuteronomy 26:1\u8211?29:9 | Haftarah: Isaiah 60:1\u8211?22 | Gospel: Matthew 4:13\u8211?24\par
\f0\fs22\i In Ki Tavo you bring the first of the harvest back because all is gift \u8212? down to the heart to understand (29:4); and the joy in it (28:47) is no atmosphere but the test of whether you still remember Who gave it.\i0\par
\par\f0\fs24 
\par\b\fs28 How to use this sheet\b0\fs24\par


\par Work from top to bottom: first observe (A1), then weigh (A2), then diagnose (A3), and only then summarize (A4). The direction \u8212? received or grasped \u8212? is the horizon, not the starting point.\par


\par\b\fs28 Basic details\b0\fs24\par


\par \b \u8594?\b0  \i First fill in the basics: which passage, which haftarah, any flanking reading with its status, and for whom you are making this.\i0 \par


\par \b Parashah / delimitation:\b0  Ki Tavo \u8212? Deuteronomy 26:1\u8211?29:9\par


\par \b Haftarah / ritual place:\b0  Isaiah 60:1\u8211?22 (sixth comfort sabbath; sheva de-nechemta)\par


\par \b Flanking reading and status:\b0  Matthew 4:13\u8211?24 \u8212? New Testament mirroring, confessionally used (not as peshat).\par


\par \b Target group and desired form:\b0  Study group / congregation \u183? a compact study and a spoken reading.\par


\par\b\fs28 A1. Text blocks and peshat\b0\fs24\par


\par \b \u8594?\b0  \i Read block by block. Note first what it says, then the key word or contrast, and only then a genuine open question \u8212? not steerable toward an answer you already want.\i0 \par










