\b Source\b0 
26:9\u8211?10 (land, fruit) \u183? 26:18 (am segulah) \u183? 29:4 (the heart)
Bearing. All is received \u8212? land, fruit, being a people, down to the heart to understand. The human receives before he brings anything back.
Why does God at times withhold the heart (29:4)?


\b Will\b0 
26:2 (bring the first) \u183? 26:5\u8211?10 (confess) \u183? 26:11 (rejoice) \u183? 27:15\u8211?26 (\u8216?Amen\u8217?)
Bearing \u8212? meets Source in thankfulness. Covenant response: bringing, confessing, remembering, obeying, rejoicing \u8212? as answer, not as source.
Where does \u8216?thankful service\u8217? turn into \u8216?my own strength\u8217? (28:47; cf. 8:17)?


\b Coherence\b0 
27:15\u8211?26 (hidden sins) \u183? 28 (blessing/curse as consequences)
Supporting; honest as second pole. Wholeness \u8212? no gap between hidden and open; blessing/curse as a coherence of consequences.
Does 27\u8211?28 pull the center of gravity away from thankfulness, or serve it?


\b Trajectory\b0 
26:1 (\u8216?when you come into the land\u8217?) \u183? 29:5 (forty years) \u183? 29:4 (\u8216?unto this day\u8217?)
Thin. From exodus to land to \u8216?this day\u8217? \u8212? pointing forward, not the core.
Is \u8216?unto this day\u8217? a limit, or a promise still opening?




\par \i Reactivity: weak; not foregrounded (\u8216?I have not transgressed nor forgotten\u8217?, 26:13, is response, not reaction). Note it as observation, and do not place it as the motor under the reading.\i0 \par


\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par \b \u8594?\b0  \i Summarize the movement: what does the text unmask, what frame does it put in its place, what response follows \u8212? and capture it in one core sentence.\i0 \par


\par \b What is unmasked?\b0  The joyless, forgetful service \u8216?for the abundance\u8217? (28:47) \u8212? the gift cut loose from the remembering of the Giver; \u8216?my own strength has gotten me this\u8217? (cf. 8:17).\par


\par \b What frame does the text put in its place?\b0  Thankful remembrance: bring the first back with the story of grace on your lips (arami oved avi), and rejoice \u8212? because all is gift, down to the heart (29:4).\par


\par \b What concrete response and formation follow?\b0  Give the first back, not the leftover; remember the story of gift aloud; share with Levite, stranger, fatherless and widow; and seek the joy as a test \u8212? do I serve out of remembrance, or out of habit?\par


\par \b Core sentence: Bringing the first back \u8212? serving out of what you received; the joy is the test of whether you still remember Who gave it.\b0 \par


\par \i \b Horizon\b0  (not this week\u8217?s theme, but the ground): beneath all this lies the one question \u8212? received or grasped. The firstfruits are the received-form; the \u8216?my own strength\u8217? service the grasped-form. In the gospel the light rises (Isa. 60; Matt. 4:16) and the eyes 29:4 still withheld open in Yeshua \u8212? the given heart, embodied.\i0 \par


